{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lily is conducting a range test on her new electric vehicle (EV). When she started her journey, the dashboard showed a full battery at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. After the first leg of the trip, the battery level dropped to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/57325e811c0dc6a9aaf80534a15cf62d74ec38b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. By the time she completed the second leg and reached her destination, the battery level had further decreased to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />. Given that the legs of the trip totaled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0362f8decbd5131e34fd0619f907ecb8be327718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers, what is the estimated total driving distance, in kilometers, of the EV on a full charge, assuming constant energy efficiency?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651b305429178af8916ec1e4810b9c0810f367d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 280\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 300\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 350\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 400\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 700$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the total driving distance on a full charge, we need to look at the total percentage of battery capacity used during the trip. Lily started with her battery at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> and finished at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, which means the entire trip consumed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fa3b51f722488cf3580ad2c903c620e6d954345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - 20\\% = 80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"14\" /> of the battery's total capacity. We are given that the total distance driven across both legs of the trip was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0362f8decbd5131e34fd0619f907ecb8be327718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers. Since the energy efficiency is constant, this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0362f8decbd5131e34fd0619f907ecb8be327718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers corresponds exactly to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7e03ccc8985ba9d029ea4add6e3e15ab9a953a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of battery capacity used. To find the total estimated distance on a full <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> charge, we can set up the proportion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e866ecec6fe6d8b716c0563e9ac4255e9c155c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{320}{0.80} = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers.\n</p><p>The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0e8603da2076aad13209af7c12bb0a4154d5ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Icosahedron0288\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems\">2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164749\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 78/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2599/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37396:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164749 and revision id 291906. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}